# Binary assets — mark them explicitly rather than relying on git's heuristic.
#
# `site/audio/` holds 1,095 MP3s. Telling git they are binary stops it attempting
# textual diffs and three-way merges on them, which is pure wasted work on a
# rebase or a large PR.
#
# NOTE: deliberately NO `filter=lfs` here. See docs/AUDIO-STORAGE-DECISION.md —
# Git LFS is a poor fit for this repository because the audio is DERIVED content
# that gets fully re-rendered from time to time, and LFS storage is cumulative:
# every re-render would permanently consume another ~206 MB of the 1 GiB free
# quota. Adding an lfs filter without the git-lfs client also leaves anyone who
# clones without it holding pointer files instead of audio.
*.mp3 binary -diff -merge
*.wav binary -diff -merge
*.png binary -diff -merge
*.jpg binary -diff -merge
*.webp binary -diff -merge
*.onnx binary -diff -merge
